      "message": "@atneya@google.com: right, this only ensures that we don\u0027t end up accessing invalid memory -- some methods may still fail (silently?) if called after the track has been stopped.\n\nAFAICT `AudioTrack` methods are synchronized internally (so we don\u0027t have races between, for example, `stop` and `setVolume`), and many of `AudioTrack` methods also check `mState`; this might be sufficient in practice?",
