      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T23:50:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After giving it some more thought I\u0027ve decided to remove the test -- it\u0027s not very reliable (it tries to trigger the race, so it depends on scheduling etc.) and takes too long.\n\nThe crash is easy to trigger manually by injecting a brief sleep in one of the TrackPlayerBase methods, for example:\n```\nstatus_t TrackPlayerBase::playerPause() {\n    if (mAudioTrack !\u003d 0) {\n        std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));\n        mAudioTrack-\u003epause();\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n... and then having thread 1 call `playerPause()` and thread 2 call `destroy()`.",
      "parentUuid": "16788d85_d2fc1e8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 55
